== two of the same thing ==
  (2, 3) == (2, 3) -> true
  (2, 3) == (9, 9) -> false
  {1, 2, 3} == {1, 2, 3} -> true
  {1, 2, 3} == {3, 2, 1} -> false
== all the way down ==
  the same route twice   -> true
  one stop moved         -> false
  a ring against a ring  -> true
== what it is not ==
  a Point and a Step, both (2, 3) -> false
  changed through a second name   -> (99, 3)
== one of them, or two ==
  first == second               -> true
  Reference.Equals(first, second) -> false
  Reference.Equals(first, alsoFirst) -> true
  after alsoFirst.Insert(4), first is {1, 2, 3, 4}
  and second is still            {1, 2, 3}
